
Tanmatra End-to-End Platform Architecture
Clean-Slate Engineering Execution Specification — P0 to Phase 13
Document status: Approved for engineering execution
Primary audience: Engineering agent, frontend lead, backend/API lead, QA agent, design-system owner, product owner
Execution model: Sequential phased delivery with mandatory phase gates
Product model: Sole-operator clinical food platform; not a multi-vendor aggregator


1. Clean-Slate Execution Directive
The engineering agent must not extend, reskin, or incrementally refactor the current product interface.
Before implementing any Tanmatra feature, the engineering agent must:

1. Archive the current repository state.
2. Audit all existing routes, components, styles, assets, dependencies, data models, state stores, and application services.
3. Classify every existing artifact as:

KEEP
REFACTOR
QUARANTINE
REMOVE



1. Remove inherited product content, legacy navigation, duplicate design systems, provider-comparison interfaces, unapproved routes, raw image usage, hard-coded commercial data, and dead interactions from the active application.
2. Move unresolved legacy code into a quarantine directory that cannot be imported by the active application.
3. Establish neutral placeholders for every approved route.
4. Complete the semantic light and dark design systems.
5. Produce a P0 completion report.
6. Begin feature implementation only after P0 and Phase 1 pass their acceptance gates.
The clean state—not the current interface—is the starting point.


