11. Non-Negotiable Domain Invariants

1. Hard allergen exclusions can never be violated by generation, Shuffle, Undo, Change Dish, Edit, or substitution.
2. A payable amount may originate only from an active server-generated quote.
3. An expired or superseded quote cannot create a new payment attempt.
4. One logical payment attempt cannot create multiple charges, orders, or subscriptions.
5. A benefit cannot be consumed before successful order creation or sponsored activation.
6. A manual meal replacement clears the plan-level Undo state.
7. Locked meals are not modified by Shuffle.
8. Checkout cannot change plan configuration.
9. Wearable information cannot change a meal without explicit user confirmation.
10. An ActiveSubscription may be created only from a confirmed subscription order or verified sponsored activation.
11. Authentication redirects must preserve the intended return route.
12. Destructive subscription actions must show delivery, financial, benefit, and renewal effects before confirmation.
13. Client state cannot author pricing, inventory, eligibility, delivery capacity, or fulfilment truth.
14. Sensitive health, employee, referral, payment, and wearable data cannot be sent to general analytics.
15. Any change affecting an active quote must invalidate or supersede the quote.
16. No silent meal substitution is permitted.
17. All unavailable actions must state why they are unavailable.
18. Checkout cannot ask plan-configuration questions that should have been resolved before quote creation.
19. A single-use entitlement must be consumed exactly once.
20. A previous meal lineup may be restored only after server-side compatibility and inventory validation.


