16. Payment Idempotency Contract
One logical payment attempt has one stable server-enforced idempotency key.
Rules:

1. Create the key when the payment attempt is created.
2. Reuse the key for network retries of the same attempt.
3. Generate a new key only after the prior attempt reaches a final state and the user explicitly initiates a new attempt.
4. Disable repeated submission while an attempt is unresolved.
5. An idempotent retry must return the existing attempt or order.
6. Entitlements are consumed only after successful activation or order creation.
7. Payment success followed by client timeout must resolve to the existing successful attempt and order.


17. Shuffle, Keep, Undo and Replacement Contract
Keep

[State Mutation: Locks the selected meal slot]


Locked meals are never changed by Shuffle.
Shuffle

[State Mutation: Regenerates unlocked meals only]


Shuffle must respect:

Hard allergens
Hard exclusions
Dietary pattern
Goal
Plan constraints
Meal slots
Inventory
Delivery date
Duplicate-frequency rules
Locked meals


Undo

[State Mutation: Restores one previous-lineup snapshot]


Only one snapshot is retained.
A second Shuffle replaces the previous snapshot.
Undo is cleared by:

Manual dish replacement
Compatibility-affecting accompaniment change
Duration change
Mealtime change
Dietary-pattern change
Goal or plan change
Location change affecting inventory
Quote creation


Undo must validate prior meals against current inventory before restoration.
Change Dish

[Action: Opens a compatible replacement sheet]


Only valid, available replacements may be selectable.
Edit

[Action: Opens accompaniment and permitted-modification sheet]


Change Dish and Edit are separate actions.


